  <div style="display: none;">
    <div id="attach_info_68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b">
      
      <div class="fancybox-video-wrapper">
        <video class="fancybox-content-video fancybox-video" controls controlsList="nodownload" poster="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b_Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video_thmb.jpg?v=72041d3b-ce62-478e-a618-c6be3eb8b939" id="player68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b" data-id="68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b" data-fileid="68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b">
          <source src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b_Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <source src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b_Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video.webm" type="video/webm" />
          Sorry, your browser doesn\'t support embedded videos, <a href="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/Adult%20Choking%20Demo%20video.mp4">download</a> and watch with your favorite video player!
          
          <script type="text/srt" id="subtitle68faa9de3d63323c95e7738b" data-label="English" data-lang="en">
            
WEBVTT

bc9e0f03-7c55-464c-b26c-228a3122e962-0
00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.222
Choking happens quickly,
so it's important to be prepared in case

bc9e0f03-7c55-464c-b26c-228a3122e962-1
00:00:04.222 --> 00:00:06.320
you need to help someone in distress.

fb7eb461-7802-4d0d-a602-152db4fbe788-0
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:11.680
Choking occurs when something gets stuck
in someone's airway and makes it hard for

fb7eb461-7802-4d0d-a602-152db4fbe788-1
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.560
them to breathe.

d5b1213c-dc88-46f6-a11a-20c228eabf35-0
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.960
A person experiencing mild choking can
still breathe, speak, and cough.

f5a22ef0-15d2-4702-aab7-3978d42094a0-0
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.760
You may not need to intervene in these
cases.

d4a5ec63-e3b4-449a-9f78-9c83f59ae748-0
00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:28.040
A person experiencing severe choking can
no longer breathe, speak, or cough.

d61acdb5-7b39-48fc-b308-415248c11ab3-0
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.040
This is an emergency.

61ea9d01-07aa-42d0-96dc-4c5e88743cc9-0
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.080
Anyone who has severely choked should be
seen by a healthcare professional.

50b89f81-05ed-4d59-9b97-09e165a9d193-0
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.320
It's not always easy to tell if someone
is choking.

89d82b4a-9de9-4408-bb71-345447b224ce-0
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.467
If you're unsure,
ask the person if they are choking and if

89d82b4a-9de9-4408-bb71-345447b224ce-1
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:43.080
you can help.

13f92195-79a3-4f33-b96f-1db4d3ccb74d-0
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:49.470
If the person's face becomes discolored,
if they're struggling to breathe or make

13f92195-79a3-4f33-b96f-1db4d3ccb74d-1
00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:52.377
sounds,
or if they're grabbing at their throat

13f92195-79a3-4f33-b96f-1db4d3ccb74d-2
00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:55.160
with their hands,
they are severely choking.

18025394-f265-4187-8e46-578ff7961229-0
00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.215
If someone else is nearby,
have them call 911 and get an AED while

18025394-f265-4187-8e46-578ff7961229-1
00:01:01.215 --> 00:01:03.720
you help the person who's choking.

6e6e3045-3a77-4534-a015-ab4e9f2c248c-0
00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:09.040
Stand firmly or kneel behind the person,
depending on your size and their size.

a0032f2a-5e84-4b5a-ba6f-43ce14ca585c-0
00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.709
Put 1 foot in front of the other to give
yourself a steady base,

a0032f2a-5e84-4b5a-ba6f-43ce14ca585c-1
00:01:14.709 --> 00:01:17.360
and place one hand on the person's
shoulder.

a9984c58-0638-43b0-b752-80441ecf2116-0
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:23.476
Then use the heel of your other hands to
give them five forceful back blows

a9984c58-0638-43b0-b752-80441ecf2116-1
00:01:23.476 --> 00:01:25.480
between the shoulder blades.

0c661cf3-47a8-49c4-ac5e-fed65a75260d-0
00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.845
This will push air from the lungs,
helping to force out the object that's

0c661cf3-47a8-49c4-ac5e-fed65a75260d-1
00:01:30.845 --> 00:01:32.080
blocking the airway.

b718fa0e-324b-469f-b9d7-aa234c0be820-0
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.400
If the five back blows do not clear the
airway, move on to abdominal thrusts.

2cd465e4-11ae-41bc-b4eb-bb8be232275c-0
00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.938
To give abdominal thrusts,
stand with your feet shoulder width apart

2cd465e4-11ae-41bc-b4eb-bb8be232275c-1
00:01:43.938 --> 00:01:46.640
and one leg slightly forward like this.

fad21042-b97e-4574-a128-d8faac314308-0
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.560
Wrap your arms around their waist so that
your hands are in front.

c20e9c06-17bc-483d-9ee4-ff20cd72e45b-0
00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:56.662
Make a fist with one hand and place it
thumb side against the person's waist,

c20e9c06-17bc-483d-9ee4-ff20cd72e45b-1
00:01:56.662 --> 00:02:00.280
just above the belly button and well
below the breastbone.

0f12712b-2354-4d6a-b9cb-8963affc8a7b-0
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.560
Now grab your fist with your other hand.

01a88aa0-6a67-4e8c-9a4c-dab664b1c04b-0
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:08.956
Next,
give quick inward and upward thrusts to

01a88aa0-6a67-4e8c-9a4c-dab664b1c04b-1
00:02:08.956 --> 00:02:12.870
the abdomen,
making sure your thrust goes upward and

01a88aa0-6a67-4e8c-9a4c-dab664b1c04b-2
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:14.200
not straight back.

12d936a6-9d2c-457a-b4aa-651110b62159-0
00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.625
Thrusting upward acts like a cough,
pushing the air out while reducing the

12d936a6-9d2c-457a-b4aa-651110b62159-1
00:02:19.625 --> 00:02:22.880
chances of causing injury to internal
organs.

9d06ede5-7fac-4ab9-a93d-74a67950ec73-0
00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:28.731
Alternate between giving 5 back blows
between the shoulder blades and five

9d06ede5-7fac-4ab9-a93d-74a67950ec73-1
00:02:28.731 --> 00:02:34.287
abdominal thrusts until the object is
forced out and the person can breathe,

9d06ede5-7fac-4ab9-a93d-74a67950ec73-2
00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:38.040
cough, or speak,
or until they become unresponsive.

696428e9-ef48-4bc7-a4b4-c6d0fbba07ee-0
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.027
If you can't wrap your arms fully around
their waist because they're larger,

696428e9-ef48-4bc7-a4b4-c6d0fbba07ee-1
00:02:44.027 --> 00:02:48.525
pregnant, or in a wheelchair,
give chest thrusts instead of abdominal

696428e9-ef48-4bc7-a4b4-c6d0fbba07ee-2
00:02:48.525 --> 00:02:49.040
thrusts.

8efa2c99-c308-4abd-a95f-c9a85b69d238-0
00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.308
In these cases,
you'll need to change your hand position

8efa2c99-c308-4abd-a95f-c9a85b69d238-1
00:02:53.308 --> 00:02:56.520
and pull back on the chest,
not up on the abdomen.

b2f0a35e-dcb3-449f-82b7-60b278001a6b-0
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:01.520
Now I'll demonstrate the correct hand
position for chest thrusts.

eccbc077-cbdd-4129-bf1e-91327e2c6d40-0
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:07.040
Make a fist with one hand and place it
thumb side against the person's torso.

cc2fedd8-9d78-4322-9fd7-147f76f960db-0
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.627
Place your arms under their armpits and
your hands in the center of their chest

cc2fedd8-9d78-4322-9fd7-147f76f960db-1
00:03:12.627 --> 00:03:14.800
on the lower half of the breastbone.

ed31c192-414b-46ae-9e19-c02127d604f2-0
00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.960
Pull straight back to give chest thrusts.

d997fc80-8669-4039-9944-8abb73254060-0
00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:23.791
If the person becomes unresponsive,
carefully slide them to the floor face up

d997fc80-8669-4039-9944-8abb73254060-1
00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:28.000
by slowly walking backward,
supporting their head and neck.

a01326c6-57ab-4023-9662-e781ace131fa-0
00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.520
Start CPR immediately and use the AED as
soon as it's available.

37aab388-baca-4bbf-b9d5-2e5388c8c3fc-0
00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:37.120
Have someone call 911 if they haven't
already done so.

6c13a0d1-954e-4046-8e48-64a3bf35d6cd-0
00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:42.235
After giving 30 chest compressions,
look in the person's mouth to check if

6c13a0d1-954e-4046-8e48-64a3bf35d6cd-1
00:03:42.235 --> 00:03:43.680
the object has come out.

48d7035d-f093-495e-8c90-7a3bc33cd1b9-0
00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.440
If you see an object, take it out.

2bd9e6e4-e6dd-4a76-b025-a5603e350fd4-0
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.307
If you can't see the object,
do not reach into their mouth to try to

2bd9e6e4-e6dd-4a76-b025-a5603e350fd4-1
00:03:51.307 --> 00:03:51.760
find it.

f59089c3-1d63-4c6e-9cec-5169e98d3a69-0
00:03:52.160 --> 00:03:57.120
You can accidentally push the object in
farther and make things worse.

358c4ddb-cff1-41ea-86f7-477dba17e74d-0
00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.240
Now that you've checked for the object,
give two breaths.

0322883b-d9f6-4ce7-ba60-c32b430b147d-0
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.893
Continue cycles of giving 30 compressions,
checking for the object,

0322883b-d9f6-4ce7-ba60-c32b430b147d-1
00:04:05.893 --> 00:04:10.693
and giving 2 breaths until emergency
responders arrive or the person starts

0322883b-d9f6-4ce7-ba60-c32b430b147d-2
00:04:10.693 --> 00:04:12.840
responding and breathing normally.

5a42a4f6-e865-48d8-89c5-9380b15bb844-0
00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:19.539
If you're alone with someone who becomes
unresponsive after choking and you do not

5a42a4f6-e865-48d8-89c5-9380b15bb844-1
00:04:19.539 --> 00:04:23.332
have a phone,
it's important to complete 5 cycles of

5a42a4f6-e865-48d8-89c5-9380b15bb844-2
00:04:23.332 --> 00:04:28.198
CPR, starting with giving 30 compressions,
checking for the object,

5a42a4f6-e865-48d8-89c5-9380b15bb844-3
00:04:28.198 --> 00:04:33.280
and then giving 2 breaths before you
leave to call 911 and get an AED.

e6a23907-81d1-4edf-b338-c01d389e0ae2-0
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.960
Now you're ready to help someone who is
choking.
          </script>
