  <div style="display: none;">
    <div id="attach_info_68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e">
      
      <div class="fancybox-video-wrapper">
        <video class="fancybox-content-video fancybox-video" controls controlsList="nodownload" poster="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e_Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video_thmb.jpg?v=18499d0c-b024-4e08-9be7-1635bb3a121d" id="player68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e" data-id="68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e" data-fileid="68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e">
          <source src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e_Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <source src="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e_Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video/Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video.webm" type="video/webm" />
          Sorry, your browser doesn\'t support embedded videos, <a href="https://iprsoftwaremedia.com/67/files/20259/Infant%20Choking%20Demo%20video.mp4">download</a> and watch with your favorite video player!
          
          <script type="text/srt" id="subtitle68faa9fc3d63323cc4e7738e" data-label="English" data-lang="en">
            
WEBVTT

4a1d2b2a-399d-4c71-b915-40362bcc3dda-0
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.666
Choking happens quickly and more often in
infants and children than in adults,

4a1d2b2a-399d-4c71-b915-40362bcc3dda-1
00:00:04.666 --> 00:00:09.000
so it's important to be prepared in case
you need to help an infant in distress.

f76009c2-7aaa-4453-befa-3b4c59251fed-0
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.395
Choking occurs when something gets stuck
in someone's airway and makes it hard for

f76009c2-7aaa-4453-befa-3b4c59251fed-1
00:00:13.395 --> 00:00:14.120
them to breathe.

423843fd-5dfe-479b-b260-ea6d4288eba8-0
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.608
An infant experiencing mild choking can
still breathe, make sounds, cry,

423843fd-5dfe-479b-b260-ea6d4288eba8-1
00:00:19.608 --> 00:00:20.240
and cough.

04a61366-6221-43fa-919a-cc8c70be3974-0
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.680
You may not need to intervene in these
cases.

6a07b202-3ada-41b9-86f2-ecf9b8cca0eb-0
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.527
An infant experiencing severe choking can
no longer breathe, make sounds, cry,

6a07b202-3ada-41b9-86f2-ecf9b8cca0eb-1
00:00:28.527 --> 00:00:29.080
or cough.

04089f2e-66ef-48f3-9ccf-8993dde71dab-0
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:30.880
This is an emergency.

3ddf48eb-8625-42d4-8839-341b8425669a-0
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:34.516
It's not always easy to tell if an infant
is choking,

3ddf48eb-8625-42d4-8839-341b8425669a-1
00:00:34.516 --> 00:00:38.763
If the infant's face becomes discolored,
if they're struggling to breathe or make

3ddf48eb-8625-42d4-8839-341b8425669a-2
00:00:38.763 --> 00:00:41.093
sounds,
or if they're tearing up or severely

3ddf48eb-8625-42d4-8839-341b8425669a-3
00:00:41.093 --> 00:00:41.560
drooling.

91e0c68e-4187-45bc-a591-75d65a7d71db-0
00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.320
They are severely choking.

50a5cb31-5c85-44be-a1a3-b7dd645bcbe7-0
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.249
If someone else is nearby,
have them call 911 and get an AED while

50a5cb31-5c85-44be-a1a3-b7dd645bcbe7-1
00:00:48.249 --> 00:00:52.200
you help the infant get into position to
provide help right away.

199d4de7-9b89-4940-b3c1-336fc16b8ac9-0
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.875
To help an infant who's choking,
you'll need to alternate between giving 5

199d4de7-9b89-4940-b3c1-336fc16b8ac9-1
00:00:56.875 --> 00:00:58.960
back blows and giving 5 chest thrusts.

f378d410-758e-477e-8338-532a01383756-0
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.346
For back blows,
place the infant face down on your

f378d410-758e-477e-8338-532a01383756-1
00:01:08.346 --> 00:01:08.840
forearm.

6147f640-4a02-4039-9c1e-e1ca2c3c2469-0
00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.800
Support the infant's head and jaw with
your hand.

b28261e3-162f-41cf-b46e-79932616ad1b-0
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.560
Rest your forearm on your lap or thigh to
support the infant.

8ae3dd0e-3538-44ca-b592-e4fe09d45cc3-0
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.320
Make sure their head is lower than the
rest of their body.

5aa687a5-27cb-4605-9592-e442a9d9f46b-0
00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.576
Then use the heel of your free hand to
give 5 firm back blows between the

5aa687a5-27cb-4605-9592-e442a9d9f46b-1
00:01:23.576 --> 00:01:24.600
shoulder blades.

4623c76c-63fb-4ea5-b436-c7bc6ea9d963-0
00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.914
This will push air from the lungs,
helping to force out the object that's

4623c76c-63fb-4ea5-b436-c7bc6ea9d963-1
00:01:28.914 --> 00:01:29.800
blocking the airway.

c94b600b-770d-4306-8491-9dd6c0c06c7b-0
00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.280
If the five back blows do not clear the
airway, move on to chest thrusts.

bfcdbecc-c76d-43d0-b569-f43bcf95bf21-0
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.920
Never give abdominal thrusts to an infant
because they can cause serious harm.

cf4cca74-cf07-4b3b-b380-7d823fc20c82-0
00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.320
Give chest thrusts instead of abdominal
thrusts.

982617c5-ab18-4723-8562-f99c5debc731-0
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.200
To give chest thrusts,
you'll need to turn the infant over.

4311932c-b52e-43cf-81ce-857f43d1b82d-0
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.896
To do this,
place your free hand on the infant's back,

4311932c-b52e-43cf-81ce-857f43d1b82d-1
00:01:49.896 --> 00:01:53.480
supporting the back of the infant's head
with the palm of your hand.

faab19fa-84f5-495d-841d-82cf5c7a5008-0
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.785
The infant will be cradled between your
forearms,

faab19fa-84f5-495d-841d-82cf5c7a5008-1
00:01:56.785 --> 00:02:00.565
with the palm of one hand supporting the
face and jaw while the palm of the other

faab19fa-84f5-495d-841d-82cf5c7a5008-2
00:02:00.565 --> 00:02:02.640
hand supports the back of the infant's
head.

0a268e21-b89d-42c5-9ef9-3e520feca95f-0
00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.200
Turn the infant over while carefully
supporting their head and neck.

5ff80809-8d13-4d78-a307-2ad55dbeeb74-0
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:11.200
Hold the infant face up with your forearm
resting on your thigh.

40418788-d247-41bf-9930-74c8e1186457-0
00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.440
Keep the infant's head lower than their
chest.

d4eb3cd5-487b-433d-aa98-1629cc671cb6-0
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.828
Place the heel of your other hand on the
lower half of the infant's breastbone,

d4eb3cd5-487b-433d-aa98-1629cc671cb6-1
00:02:19.828 --> 00:02:21.120
just below the ****** line.

fefe9b34-972c-4c40-963a-a52bf7c238aa-0
00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.683
Push downward on the middle of the chest
five times at a rate of about 1 thrust

fefe9b34-972c-4c40-963a-a52bf7c238aa-1
00:02:26.683 --> 00:02:29.460
per second,
creating enough force to dislodge the

fefe9b34-972c-4c40-963a-a52bf7c238aa-2
00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:30.960
object blocking the airway.

ceda1079-9c46-4214-a3b1-16c14ac01e01-0
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:36.836
Alternate between giving 5 back blows and
five chest thrusts until the object is

ceda1079-9c46-4214-a3b1-16c14ac01e01-1
00:02:36.836 --> 00:02:39.513
forced out and the infant can breathe or
cough,

ceda1079-9c46-4214-a3b1-16c14ac01e01-2
00:02:39.513 --> 00:02:41.800
or until the infant becomes unresponsive.

a2f35fa7-ef37-4534-bcb7-49c0708d1077-0
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.854
If the infant becomes unresponsive,
place them face up on a firm,

a2f35fa7-ef37-4534-bcb7-49c0708d1077-1
00:02:47.854 --> 00:02:50.440
flat surface and start CPR immediately.

962e1171-02ef-4a30-8eb9-323a81422a34-0
00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.200
Use the AED as soon as it's available.

406a9005-1fd7-47ce-a15d-ab0963e23048-0
00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.520
Have someone call 911 if they haven't
already done so.


f2620f50-8169-4ef8-a2e5-54c8e190181e-0
00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.725
After giving 30 chest compressions,
look in the infant's mouth to check if

f2620f50-8169-4ef8-a2e5-54c8e190181e-1
00:03:05.725 --> 00:03:06.870
the object has come out.

b4635748-804e-4adf-b4a1-abb7851e846e-0
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.630
If you see an object, take it out.

31a50d9c-308c-44c9-a9cf-b05f65673ed7-0
00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:13.679
If you can't see the object,
do not reach into their mouth to try to

31a50d9c-308c-44c9-a9cf-b05f65673ed7-1
00:03:13.679 --> 00:03:14.070
find it.

8e19e9aa-ede2-435f-a538-e32ce3ade6bd-0
00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:17.990
You can accidentally push the object in
farther and make things worse.

5ee2ca34-be9e-4c74-bf7b-91f510e363b4-0
00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:21.590
If the object did not come out,
give 2 breaths.

1c5e3ab5-2865-4cf1-90ab-a0eaea62d34e-0
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.316
Continue cycles of giving 30 compressions,
checking for the object,

1c5e3ab5-2865-4cf1-90ab-a0eaea62d34e-1
00:03:26.316 --> 00:03:30.641
and giving 2 breaths until the emergency
responders arrive or the infant starts

1c5e3ab5-2865-4cf1-90ab-a0eaea62d34e-2
00:03:30.641 --> 00:03:32.480
responding and breathing normally.

78ff8a84-b5ef-43c2-b513-beadf6be2604-0
00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.180
If you're alone with an infant who
becomes unresponsive after choking and

78ff8a84-b5ef-43c2-b513-beadf6be2604-1
00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.692
you do not have a phone,
it's important to complete 5 cycles of

78ff8a84-b5ef-43c2-b513-beadf6be2604-2
00:03:40.692 --> 00:03:44.423
CPR, starting with giving 30 compressions,
checking for the object,

78ff8a84-b5ef-43c2-b513-beadf6be2604-3
00:03:44.423 --> 00:03:48.320
and then giving 2 breaths before you
leave to call 911 and get an AED.

124a3d65-6fdf-468b-8887-b1678338367a-0
00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:52.364
No matter what,
any infant who receives choking relief

124a3d65-6fdf-468b-8887-b1678338367a-1
00:03:52.364 --> 00:03:54.800
should be seen by a healthcare
rofessional.

12ae830d-10f5-43ae-b3ca-c590946390cc-0
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.760
Now you're ready to help an infant who is
choking.
          </script>
